      "reasoning": "The student needs to relate the smaller triangle (AMN) to the larger triangle (PMN). I will use the analogy of a shadow cast by a building to help them visualize the relationship between the height (PN) and the base (MN). [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"15 * tan(21 * 3.14159 / 180)\") -> 5.758]",
      "content": "Think of this like a building casting a shadow. $\\text{MN}$ is the distance from the building, and $\\text{PN}$ is the height of the building. $\\text{A}$ is a point halfway up the building. \n\nIf you look at the smaller triangle $\\Delta\\text{AMN}$, you have the base ($15$) and the angle ($21^\\circ$). Using the tangent ratio, how would you calculate the height $\\text{AN}$?"
